Id: con016e
Severity: ERROR
Category: tigris
Check: config
Fix: chmod go-w the file and chown it to root, or name one that is; then run again.
References: tigris(8); tigris.conf

The configuration file named with -c failed the check every
configuration file gets before it is read: it is writable by its group
or by others, or it belongs to someone other than root, the user running
Tigris or the owner of Tigris's own files (con003c, con015c, printed
just before). A configuration file is run as shell code by whoever runs
Tigris, root as a rule, so one that others can change is theirs to run.
A file Tigris finds on its own is skipped for the next candidate; a file
named with -c has no next candidate, and running every check instead is
not what -c asked for, so the run stops.
